WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
As a young man, Augustine of
Hippo followed the Manichees.

2
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.850
They taught two equal
powers: Light and Darkness,

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.560
Good and Evil.

4
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.720
Augustine came to reject this.

5
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:16.120
There is one God, he said, and
everything God made is good.

6
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.790
Genesis agrees: God saw
everything he had made,

7
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.620
and it was very good.

8
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.000
So if God made everything,
and all of it was good,

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.020
where did evil come from?

10
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.320
In this mission, you'll follow Augustine's
account of the fall of angels and of

11
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:32.350
humans.

12
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.200
Then you'll put his theodicy
on trial: against logic,

13
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.340
against evolution, and against Hell.

14
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.200
Your mission: explain where
Augustine says evil came from,

15
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.010
and whether that clears God.
